  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Katama Dam project in Kitui Supported by Five Talents UK</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To conduct an assessment with the community in Katama in Kitui, Kenya. The baseline survey will seek to identify
the community&apos;s desired outcomes of the water project, history of interventions and why these failed and the
community&#x2019;s willingness to contribute (labour and basic materials). The dam survey will identify the best solution
(whether to use the existing dam or a new site) and refine the technical details. These two assessments will be
detailed by CAFOD in a report to EDCDT and Five Talents UK before the next steps for the project are agreed by
all parties.
The project will focus on providing a working earth dam for the community in Katama. Depending on the results
of the assessment, this will either be by creating a new dam, or improving an existing dam that is currently not
working.</narrative>
  </description>
